---
import {selectMentionNetwork} from '../../lib/corpus/mention-network-layout.mjs';
interface Props { projection: any; }
const {projection}=Astro.props;
const d=projection.data;
const fmt=(n:number|null,digits=2)=>n===null?'Unavailable':n.toLocaleString('en-GB',{maximumFractionDigits:digits});
const initialName=d.names[0]?.name;
const initialEdges=selectMentionNetwork(d).edges;
const safeJson=JSON.stringify(projection).replaceAll('<','\\u003c').replaceAll('>','\\u003e').replaceAll('&','\\u0026');
---
<section class="network-dynamics" id="mention-dynamics" aria-labelledby="network-title">
  <header>
    <p class="corpus-eyebrow">Exploratory text research</p>
    <h2 id="network-title">Names in the archive: patterns over time</h2>
    <p>Explore the spread of tracked names and which names occur near each other. These are patterns in the selected transcripts—not a social network, evidence of relationships, or findings about anyone’s personality.</p>
  </header>
  <aside class="network-warning">
    <strong>Machine-generated and unreviewed; may be wrong; not a verified quotation.</strong>
    <p>Name matching is heuristic and incomplete. Selected Daniel-labelled and unlabelled text may contain other people, quotations, playback or viewer messages; unlabelled speech is not attributed to Daniel. Matching weights are not measured probabilities that a reference is correct.</p>
  </aside>
  <dl class="network-kpis">
    <div><dt>Transcript renditions retained</dt><dd>{fmt(d.counts.retained_recordings,0)}<small>{fmt(d.counts.recordings,0)} considered before exact-text exclusions</small></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Tracked public labels</dt><dd>{d.names.length}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Weighted name matches</dt><dd>{fmt(d.counts.weighted_matches,0)}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Undated recordings</dt><dd>{fmt(d.counts.undated_recordings,0)}<small>Excluded from calendar charts</small></dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p class="network-scope">{fmt(d.counts.labelled_words,0)} eligible words have a selected Daniel label; {fmt(d.counts.unlabelled_words,0)} have no assigned speaker. Neither a label nor an explicit name match proves who spoke or whom it refers to.</p>
  {d.counts.ambiguous_duplicate_date_groups>0&&<p class="network-scope">{fmt(d.counts.ambiguous_duplicate_date_groups,0)} identical-transcript groups have inconsistent or partly missing date metadata and are treated as undated in the main calendar series.</p>}
  <nav class="network-jumps" aria-label="Mention research sections">
    <a href="#network-spread">Spread over time</a><a href="#network-links">Co-mentions</a><a href="#network-attention">Name trends</a><a href="#network-methods">Methods &amp; limitations</a>
  </nav>
  <noscript><p>JavaScript is required for chart controls. The expandable value tables below remain available without it.</p></noscript>

  <section class="network-panel" id="network-spread" aria-labelledby="spread-title">
    <h3 id="spread-title">How concentrated are the tracked on-channel names?</h3>
    <p>Higher spread means matches are distributed more evenly across the tracked labels; lower spread means fewer names dominate. This curated group includes names used on the channel, handles and pets, not an inferred personal circle. Public-creator labels are excluded from this measure.</p>
    <div class="network-controls"><label>Measure <select data-spread-select><option value="spread">Spread of name matches (0–1)</option><option value="top_share">Most-mentioned name’s share</option><option value="active_names">Names with at least five weighted matches</option><option value="rate">Weighted matches per 10,000 words</option></select></label></div>
    <figure><div data-spread-chart class="network-chart" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable annual name-match chart"></div><figcaption>Shaded bands are conditional 95% resampling ranges—not confidence in identities or transcript accuracy. Weighted point estimates can fall outside these ranges. Sparse years must be read with their word coverage below.</figcaption></figure>
    <details><summary>Annual values and source coverage</summary><div class="network-table-scroll"><table><caption>Tracked on-channel label concentration by recording year</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">Eligible words</th><th scope="col">Spread [conditional 95% range]</th><th scope="col">Top-name share</th><th scope="col">Active names</th><th scope="col">Matches / 10k words</th></tr></thead><tbody>{d.annual.map((r:any)=><tr><th scope="row">{r.year}</th><td>{fmt(r.words,0)}</td><td>{fmt(r.spread[1])} [{fmt(r.spread[0])}–{fmt(r.spread[2])}]</td><td>{fmt(r.top_share[1])}</td><td>{fmt(r.active_names[1],0)}</td><td>{fmt(r.rate[1])}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
    {d.annual.some((r:any)=>r.all_renditions_words!==null)&&<details><summary>Compare exact-transcript exclusions with all renditions retained</summary><p>The main series collapses identical selected public transcript sequences. Where their date metadata is inconsistent or partly missing, the retained content is left undated. The comparison retains every rendition with its original admitted date metadata. Differences reflect repeated transcript weight and date choices together—not a validated count of distinct videos.</p><div class="network-table-scroll"><table><caption>Same matching rules: main versus all-renditions scenario</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">Main eligible words</th><th scope="col">All-renditions words</th><th scope="col">Main spread</th><th scope="col">All-renditions spread</th><th scope="col">Main rate / 10k</th><th scope="col">All-renditions rate / 10k</th></tr></thead><tbody>{d.annual.map((r:any)=><tr><th scope="row">{r.year}</th><td>{fmt(r.words,0)}</td><td>{fmt(r.all_renditions_words,0)}</td><td>{fmt(r.spread[1])}</td><td>{fmt(r.all_renditions_spread)}</td><td>{fmt(r.rate[1])}</td><td>{fmt(r.all_renditions_rate)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>}
  </section>

  <section class="network-panel" id="network-links" aria-labelledby="links-title">
    <h3 id="links-title">Which names are mentioned near each other?</h3>
    <p>A link means two tracked names appear within the same two-minute window. It does not imply the people know each other, were present, agree, or participated together. Layout and proximity are illustrative, not additional evidence.</p>
    <div class="network-controls network-focus-controls"><label>Find a name and explore its links <input type="search" data-network-focus list="mention-network-labels" placeholder="All tracked labels" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="network-controls-help"/><datalist id="mention-network-labels">{d.names.map((n:any)=><option value={n.name}/>)}</datalist></label><button type="button" data-network-overview>Show overview</button><button type="button" data-network-reset>Reset all filters</button></div>
    <p id="network-controls-help" class="network-muted">Choose a complete tracked label or select a node to focus on its direct co-mention links. Clear the name to return to the overview. Filters change this illustration and its values table, not the underlying research.</p>
    <div class="network-controls network-map-controls"><label>Label group <select data-network-group><option value="all">All tracked labels</option><option value="on_channel">Curated on-channel labels</option><option value="public_creator">Public creators</option></select></label><label>Minimum weighted co-mentions <select data-network-support><option value="0">All published links</option><option value="5" selected>5</option><option value="10">10</option><option value="25">25</option><option value="50">50</option></select></label><label>Minimum lift above baseline <select data-network-lift><option value="1">1×</option><option value="1.5" selected>1.5×</option><option value="2">2×</option><option value="3">3×</option><option value="5">5×</option></select></label><label>Clutter limit <select data-network-limit><option value="20">Strongest 20 links</option><option value="40" selected>Strongest 40 links</option><option value="80">Strongest 80 links</option><option value="1000">All qualifying links</option></select></label></div>
    <details><summary>Which links are included?</summary><p class="network-muted">The aggregate includes links with at least three weighted co-mentions. “All published links” removes only the extra support filter; it cannot restore lower-support links omitted from the aggregate. The label-group, lift and clutter filters still apply.</p></details>
    <p class="network-muted" data-network-count aria-live="polite"></p>
    <ul class="network-legend" aria-label="Co-mention map legend"><li><span class="legend-circle" aria-hidden="true"></span> Circle: curated on-channel label (includes handles and pets)</li><li><span class="legend-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></span> Triangle: public-creator label</li><li><span class="legend-edge" aria-hidden="true"></span> Thicker link: more weighted co-mentions, not higher lift</li><li>Larger node: more weighted co-mentions among displayed links</li></ul>
    <div class="network-controls network-view-controls" aria-label="Map view controls"><button type="button" data-map-zoom-out aria-label="Zoom map out">−</button><button type="button" data-map-zoom-in aria-label="Zoom map in">+</button><button type="button" data-map-fit>Fit map</button><button type="button" data-map-reset-view>Reset view</button><button type="button" data-map-reset-layout>Reset layout</button><span data-map-zoom aria-label="Map magnification">100%</span></div>
    <p id="network-interaction-help" class="network-muted">Drag nodes or pan empty space; wheel/pinch zooms. Arrow keys move a focused node or pan the focused map; + / − zoom and 0 fits. Click/tap or Enter/Space focuses a name. View and layout resets keep your data filters.</p>
    <figure><div data-network-chart class="network-chart" tabindex="0" aria-label="Interactive co-mention map" aria-describedby="network-interaction-help"></div><figcaption>Connection-driven layout places connected names near each other and separates disconnected parts of the displayed map. Dragging changes only the illustration. Shapes and colors indicate curated label groups—not inferred social communities. Node size uses displayed weighted degree; it changes with filters. Lift compares the count with a within-recording circular-shift baseline; the filter is descriptive, not a significance test.</figcaption></figure>
    <details><summary>Co-mention values (accessible alternative to the graph)</summary><div class="network-table-scroll network-long-table" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable co-mention values"><table><caption data-network-caption>Strongest 40 qualifying links: at least 5 weighted co-mentions and 1.5× baseline</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Weighted co-mentions</th><th scope="col">Baseline</th><th scope="col">Lift</th></tr></thead><tbody data-network-rows>{initialEdges.map((e:any)=><tr><th scope="row">{e.a}</th><td>{e.b}</td><td>{fmt(e.weight,1)}</td><td>{fmt(e.baseline,1)}</td><td>{fmt(e.lift)}×</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
  </section>

  <section class="network-panel" id="network-attention" aria-labelledby="attention-title">
    <h3 id="attention-title">Follow a tracked name over time</h3>
    <p>Weighted matches per 10,000 eligible words, by recording month. A zero means no retained match—not that someone was absent. Months with fewer than three recordings are omitted from the chart. Unknown recording dates are not replaced with upload dates.</p>
    <div class="network-controls"><label>Tracked label <select data-name-select>{d.names.map((n:any)=><option value={n.name}>{n.name}</option>)}</select></label></div>
    <figure><div data-name-chart class="network-chart" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable monthly name-match chart"></div><figcaption>Changes can reflect archive coverage, recording format, transcript engines, spelling, or conversation topic. A peak is not a dated event or an independently verified life change.</figcaption></figure>
    <details><summary>Monthly rates and source coverage</summary><div class="network-table-scroll network-long-table"><table><caption data-monthly-caption>{initialName}: monthly name matches</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Recording month</th><th scope="col">Matches / 10k words</th><th scope="col">Recordings</th><th scope="col">Project-cloud transcript share</th></tr></thead><tbody data-monthly-rows>{d.monthly.map((r:any)=><tr><th scope="row">{r.month}</th><td>{fmt(r.rates[initialName])}{r.recordings<3?' (sparse month)':''}</td><td>{fmt(r.recordings,0)}</td><td>{r.own_job_share===null?'Unavailable':`${fmt(r.own_job_share*100,1)}%`}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
    {d.sensitivity.length>0&&<details><summary>How much does removing question-shaped name matches change this series?</summary><p>This aligned sensitivity check uses the same admitted transcripts, duplicate exclusions and word denominator. It removes name matches in question-shaped segments; questions can be genuine dialogue, and viewer readouts can be non-questions. Neither scenario identifies the speaker or reliably isolates viewer messages.</p><div class="network-table-scroll"><table><caption data-sensitivity-caption>{initialName}: annual name rates, main versus question-filtered scenario</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">Main rate / 10k words</th><th scope="col">Question-filtered rate / 10k words</th></tr></thead><tbody data-sensitivity-rows>{d.sensitivity.map((r:any)=><tr><th scope="row">{r.year}</th><td>{fmt(r.rates[initialName][0])}</td><td>{fmt(r.rates[initialName][1])}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>}
    {d.bursts.length>0&&<details><summary>Heuristic high-rate episodes for the selected name</summary><p>A flagged month has at least ten weighted matches and three recordings, with a rate at least three times the surrounding ±12-calendar-month median (at least three eligible neighbour months; baseline floor 0.2 per 10,000 words). Adjacent calendar months are grouped. These thresholds are descriptive—not a significance test, a life-event date, or a prediction.</p><div class="network-table-scroll"><table><caption data-burst-caption>{initialName}: heuristic high-rate episodes</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">First recording month</th><th scope="col">Last recording month</th><th scope="col">Consecutive months</th></tr></thead><tbody data-burst-rows>{d.bursts.filter((r:any)=>r.name===initialName).map((r:any)=><tr><th scope="row">{r.start}</th><td>{r.end}</td><td>{r.months}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>}
  </section>

  {d.shifts.length>0&&<section class="network-panel"><h3>Candidate changes in the mix of names</h3><p>These preselected months compare the name mix in six calendar months before and after. Percentile ranks are relative to other testable months in this archive; neither the rank nor a small permutation p-value establishes a cause or a life event.</p><details><summary>Show candidate-month comparisons</summary><div class="network-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">Excess divergence</th><th scope="col">Archive percentile</th><th scope="col">Uncorrected permutation p</th></tr></thead><tbody>{d.shifts.map((r:any)=><tr><th scope="row">{r.month}</th><td>{fmt(r.excess,3)}</td><td>{fmt(r.percentile,1)}</td><td>{fmt(r.permutation_p,3)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details></section>}

  <section class="network-panel" id="network-methods">
    <h3>Methods, coverage and uncertainty</h3>
    <p>This is descriptive, heuristic research on admitted public transcript text. It is separate from the sourced wiki and does not verify the wording, identify unnamed speakers, infer private relationships, or evaluate a person.</p>
    <details><summary>How the estimates are constructed</summary>
      <ul><li>Explicit name strings and selected spelling variants are matched using contextual rules and hand-set weights. Pronouns and roles such as “my mum” are not resolved to people; ambiguous names and aliases can be wrong.</li><li>Eligibility excludes other explicitly labelled speakers, playback, text-to-speech and uncertain audio where marked. Unlabelled material remains unidentified, and automatic readout filtering is incomplete.</li><li>{fmt(d.counts.duplicate_transcript_exclusions,0)} identical selected public transcript renditions are excluded by matching their segment text, timing and labels. This does not prove that their complete media or recording identities are identical.</li><li>Rates use eligible transcript words, not recording duration or real-world attention. Recording dates come from corpus metadata and may themselves be uncertain.</li><li>{fmt(d.counts.draws,0)} resampling draws combine matching weights with recording resampling. Ranges are conditional on those assumptions; they exclude unknown ASR errors, registry mistakes, unresolved speakers and missing recordings. They are not calibrated probabilities or prediction intervals.</li><li>The co-mention baseline circularly shifts each name’s positions within a recording, retaining within-name temporal clustering. Lift is a descriptive comparison, not a corrected statistical test.</li><li>Model-rated per-person tone, diagnostic interpretations, alleged relationships, early-warning predictions and historical model-score joins are not presented. Heuristic high-rate episodes describe only the retained text and recording-date metadata.</li></ul>
    </details>
    {d.agreement.length>0&&<details><summary>Transcript-source agreement checks</summary><p>Different transcripts of the same candidate recordings can produce different name matches. Agreement is not identity verification or ground-truth accuracy.</p><div class="network-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Label</th><th scope="col">Compared recordings</th><th scope="col">Presence agreement</th><th scope="col">Rank correlation</th></tr></thead><tbody>{d.agreement.map((r:any)=><tr><th scope="row">{r.name}</th><td>{fmt(r.recordings,0)}</td><td>{fmt(r.presence_agreement)}</td><td>{fmt(r.rank_correlation)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>}
    <details><summary>Snapshot and reproducibility bindings</summary><dl class="network-provenance"><div><dt>Generated</dt><dd>{projection.generated_at}</dd></div><div><dt>Corpus release</dt><dd>{projection.binding.corpus_release}</dd></div><div><dt>Summary release</dt><dd>{projection.binding.summary_release}</dd></div><div><dt>Source archive checksum</dt><dd>{projection.binding.corpus_archive_sha256}</dd></div><div><dt>Corpus manifest checksum</dt><dd>{projection.binding.corpus_manifest_sha256}</dd></div><div><dt>Transcript input digest</dt><dd>{projection.binding.transcript_input_sha256}</dd></div><div><dt>Name-registry checksum</dt><dd>{projection.binding.registry_sha256}</dd></div><div><dt>Builder checksum</dt><dd>{projection.binding.builder_sha256}</dd></div><div><dt>Methods</dt><dd>{projection.binding.method_version}</dd></div><div><dt>Aggregate payload checksum</dt><dd>{projection.payload_sha256}</dd></div></dl><p>Only this validated aggregate projection is included here. Research excerpts, samples, raw media, private review records and voice/face data are not included. This text-only study does not join historical model-rated passage scores.</p></details>
  </section>
  <script is:inline type="application/json" data-network-data set:html={safeJson}></script>
</section>

<script>
  import {selectMentionNetwork,layoutMentionNetwork} from '../../lib/corpus/mention-network-layout.mjs';
  import {attachMentionMapInteraction} from '../../lib/corpus/mention-network-interaction.mjs';
  const ns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.network-dynamics').forEach(root=>{
    const raw=root.querySelector('[data-network-data]')?.textContent;if(!raw)return;
    const data=JSON.parse(raw).data;
    const q=(s:string)=>root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(s)!;
    const fmt=(n:number|null,d=2)=>n===null?'Unavailable':n.toLocaleString('en-GB',{maximumFractionDigits:d});
    const element=(tag:string,attrs:Record<string,string|number>,parent:Element,text?:string)=>{const e=document.createElementNS(ns,tag);for(const [k,v] of Object.entries(attrs))e.setAttribute(k,String(v));if(text)e.textContent=text;parent.append(e);return e;};
    const svg=(host:HTMLElement,height:number,label:string,width=900)=>{host.replaceChildren();const s=element('svg',{viewBox:`0 0 ${width} ${height}`,role:'img','aria-label':label},host);element('title',{},s,label);return s;};
    const chart=(host:HTMLElement,rows:any[],label:string,max?:number)=>{
      const s=svg(host,260,label);const values=rows.flatMap(r=>[r.value,r.low,r.high]).filter(v=>typeof v==='number'&&Number.isFinite(v));
      if(!values.length){element('text',{x:20,y:50},s,'No eligible values for this view.');return;}
      const top=max??Math.max(1,...values)*1.05;const x=(i:number)=>55+i*820/Math.max(1,rows.length-1),y=(v:number)=>225-v/top*200;
      for(let i=0;i<5;i++){const v=i*top/4;element('line',{x1:55,x2:875,y1:y(v),y2:y(v),class:'chart-grid'},s);element('text',{x:48,y:y(v)+4,'text-anchor':'end',class:'chart-axis'},s,fmt(v));}
      // Split paths at excluded months: never connect across a coverage gap.
      let path='';let last=false;rows.forEach((r,i)=>{if(r.value===null){last=false;return;}path+=`${last?'L':'M'}${x(i)},${y(r.value)} `;last=true;});
      element('path',{d:path,fill:'none',class:'chart-line'},s);
      rows.forEach((r,i)=>{if(r.low!==null&&r.high!==null)element('line',{x1:x(i),x2:x(i),y1:y(r.low),y2:y(r.high),class:'chart-band'},s);if(r.value!==null){const circle=element('circle',{cx:x(i),cy:y(r.value),r:3,class:'chart-point'},s);element('title',{},circle,`${r.label}: ${fmt(r.value)}${r.low===null?'':` [${fmt(r.low)}–${fmt(r.high)}]`}`);}if(rows.length<20||r.label.endsWith('-01'))element('text',{x:x(i),y:247,'text-anchor':'middle',class:'chart-axis'},s,rows.length<20?r.label:r.label.slice(0,4));});
    };
    const spread=()=>{const select=q('[data-spread-select]') as HTMLSelectElement;const key=select.value;chart(q('[data-spread-chart]'),data.annual.map((r:any)=>({label:String(r.year),low:r[key][0],value:r[key][1],high:r[key][2]})),select.selectedOptions[0].textContent||key,['spread','top_share'].includes(key)?1:undefined);};
    q('[data-spread-select]').addEventListener('change',spread);spread();
    const row=(values:string[],parent:HTMLElement)=>{const tr=document.createElement('tr');values.forEach((value,i)=>{const cell=document.createElement(i===0?'th':'td');if(i===0)cell.setAttribute('scope','row');cell.textContent=value;tr.append(cell);});parent.append(tr);};
    const name=()=>{
      const selected=(q('[data-name-select]') as HTMLSelectElement).value;
      chart(q('[data-name-chart]'),data.monthly.map((r:any)=>({label:r.month,value:r.recordings>=3?r.rates[selected]:null,low:null,high:null})),`${selected}: weighted name matches per 10,000 eligible words`);
      const body=q('[data-monthly-rows]');body.replaceChildren();q('[data-monthly-caption]').textContent=`${selected}: monthly name-match rates and coverage`;
      data.monthly.forEach((r:any)=>row([r.month,`${fmt(r.rates[selected])}${r.recordings<3?' (sparse month)':''}`,fmt(r.recordings,0),r.own_job_share===null?'Unavailable':`${fmt(r.own_job_share*100,1)}%`],body));
      if(data.sensitivity.length){const rows=q('[data-sensitivity-rows]');rows.replaceChildren();q('[data-sensitivity-caption]').textContent=`${selected}: main versus question-filtered annual rates`;data.sensitivity.forEach((r:any)=>row([String(r.year),fmt(r.rates[selected][0]),fmt(r.rates[selected][1])],rows));}
      if(data.bursts.length){const rows=q('[data-burst-rows]');rows.replaceChildren();q('[data-burst-caption]').textContent=`${selected}: heuristic high-rate episodes`;const episodes=data.bursts.filter((r:any)=>r.name===selected);if(!episodes.length)row(['No episodes meet these thresholds.','',''],rows);else episodes.forEach((r:any)=>row([r.start,r.end,String(r.months)],rows));}
    };
    q('[data-name-select]').addEventListener('change',name);name();
    const focusInput=q('[data-network-focus]') as HTMLInputElement;
    let mapView:ReturnType<typeof attachMentionMapInteraction>|undefined;
    let lastMapWidth=0;
    const network=()=>{
      mapView?.destroy();
      const controls={group:(q('[data-network-group]') as HTMLSelectElement).value,minLift:Number((q('[data-network-lift]') as HTMLSelectElement).value),minSupport:Number((q('[data-network-support]') as HTMLSelectElement).value),maxEdges:Number((q('[data-network-limit]') as HTMLSelectElement).value),focus:focusInput.value};
      const selection=selectMentionNetwork(data,controls);
      lastMapWidth=q('[data-network-chart]').clientWidth;
      const layout=layoutMentionNetwork(selection,{width:Math.max(300,lastMapWidth)});
      const {nodes,edges}=selection;
      let message=`${selection.focus?`${selection.focus}: direct co-mentions · `:''}${nodes.length} labels · showing ${edges.length} of ${selection.eligibleEdges} qualifying links`;
      if(selection.hiddenEdges)message+=` · ${selection.hiddenEdges} lower-support links hidden by the clutter limit`;
      if(selection.reason==='unknown_focus')message='Choose a complete tracked label from the suggestions, or clear the name to show the overview.';
      if(selection.reason==='excluded_focus')message=`${selection.focus} is outside the selected label group. Choose “All tracked labels” to explore its links.`;
      if(selection.reason==='no_edges')message=`${selection.focus?`No displayed links for ${selection.focus}. `:'No links meet these filters. '}Lower the minimum weighted co-mentions or lift, choose a wider label group, or reset all filters.`;
      q('[data-network-count]').textContent=message;
      q('[data-network-caption]').textContent=`${selection.focus?`${selection.focus}: `:''}Displayed co-mention links, ranked by support · minimum ${controls.minSupport} weighted co-mentions and ${controls.minLift}× baseline`;
      const body=q('[data-network-rows]');body.replaceChildren();if(!edges.length)row([message,'','','',''],body);else edges.forEach((e:any)=>row([e.a,e.b,fmt(e.weight,1),fmt(e.baseline,1),`${fmt(e.lift)}×`],body));
      const s=svg(q('[data-network-chart]'),layout.height,'Interactive illustrative co-mention map. Select a node to focus on its links. All values are available in the table below.',layout.width);s.setAttribute('role','group');s.setAttribute('style',`height:${layout.height}px`);
      const layer=element('g',{'data-map-layer':''},s);
      if(!edges.length)element('text',{x:24,y:52,class:'chart-axis'},layer,'No map for these filters.');
      const positions=new Map(layout.nodes.map((n:any)=>[n.name,n]));const maxSupport=Math.max(1,...edges.map((e:any)=>e.weight));const maxDegree=Math.max(1,...nodes.map((n:any)=>n.degree));
      const interactiveEdges=edges.map((e:any)=>{const a=positions.get(e.a)!,b=positions.get(e.b)!;const line=element('line',{x1:a.x,y1:a.y,x2:b.x,y2:b.y,class:'network-edge','stroke-width':1+6*Math.sqrt(e.weight/maxSupport)},layer);element('title',{},line,`${e.a} / ${e.b}: ${fmt(e.weight)} weighted co-mentions, ${fmt(e.lift)}× baseline`);return {...e,element:line};});
      const choose=(name:string,restoreFocus=false)=>{focusInput.value=name;network();if(restoreFocus){const node=[...q('[data-network-chart]').querySelectorAll<SVGElement>('[data-node-name]')].find(n=>n.getAttribute('data-node-name')===name);node?.focus();}};
      const interactiveNodes=layout.nodes.map((n:any)=>{
        const radius=Math.max(5,20*Math.sqrt(n.degree/maxDegree));const group=n.group==='public_creator'?'creator':'on-channel';
        const g=element('g',{class:`network-node-button ${group}${n.focused?' focused':''}`,tabindex:0,role:'button','aria-label':`Focus on ${n.name}. ${n.links} displayed links; weighted degree ${fmt(n.degree,1)}.`,'aria-pressed':String(n.focused),'data-node-name':n.name},layer);
        if(group==='creator')element('path',{d:`M${n.x},${n.y-radius} L${n.x-radius},${n.y+radius*.75} L${n.x+radius},${n.y+radius*.75} Z`,class:'network-node'},g);else element('circle',{cx:n.x,cy:n.y,r:radius,class:'network-node'},g);
        if(Math.abs(n.labelY-(n.y+4))>16)element('line',{x1:n.x,y1:n.y,x2:n.labelX,y2:n.labelY-4,class:'network-label-leader'},g);
        element('text',{x:n.labelX,y:n.labelY,class:'network-label'},g,n.name);
        element('title',{},g,`${n.name}: ${n.links} displayed links; ${fmt(n.degree,1)} weighted co-mentions. Select to focus.`);
        return {...n,element:g};
      });
      mapView=attachMentionMapInteraction(s,layer,{width:layout.width,height:layout.height,nodes:interactiveNodes,edges:interactiveEdges,onActivate:choose,onViewChange:(view:any)=>{q('[data-map-zoom]').textContent=`${Math.round(view.scale*100)}%`;}});
    };
    for(const selector of ['[data-network-group]','[data-network-lift]','[data-network-support]','[data-network-limit]'])q(selector).addEventListener('change',network);
    focusInput.addEventListener('input',network);
    q('[data-network-overview]').addEventListener('click',()=>{focusInput.value='';network();});
    q('[data-network-reset]').addEventListener('click',()=>{focusInput.value='';(q('[data-network-group]') as HTMLSelectElement).value='all';(q('[data-network-lift]') as HTMLSelectElement).value='1.5';(q('[data-network-support]') as HTMLSelectElement).value='5';(q('[data-network-limit]') as HTMLSelectElement).value='40';network();});
    q('[data-map-zoom-in]').addEventListener('click',()=>mapView?.zoom(1.25));q('[data-map-zoom-out]').addEventListener('click',()=>mapView?.zoom(.8));q('[data-map-fit]').addEventListener('click',()=>mapView?.fit());q('[data-map-reset-view]').addEventListener('click',()=>mapView?.resetView());q('[data-map-reset-layout]').addEventListener('click',network);
    network();
    if(typeof ResizeObserver!=='undefined'){let resizeTimer:ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>;new ResizeObserver(()=>{if(Math.abs(q('[data-network-chart]').clientWidth-lastMapWidth)>1){clearTimeout(resizeTimer);resizeTimer=setTimeout(network,150);}}).observe(q('[data-network-chart]'));}
  });
</script>

